        ss_o >> val_g_re >> val_g_im;  // from ref_output.txt
        real_dtype val_a_re = s2mm_bo_mapped[ss];
        real_dtype val_a_im = s2mm_bo_mapped[ss + 1];
        ss_a << val_a_re << " " << val_a_im << std::endl;
        real_dtype err_re = abs(val_g_re - val_a_re);
        real_dtype err_im = abs(val_g_im - val_a_im);
        bool this_flag = (err_re > level) || (err_im > level); // Reference model is not bit accurate
        ...
        flag |= this_flag;
    }
}
...
if (flag == 0) ... PASSED ...
else ... FAILED ...
```

So `level = (1 << 8) = 256`. The error threshold is 256 (absolute error in the integer representation of the fixed-point/integer output). If either real or imaginary error exceeds 256, it's flagged. Note the comment "Reference model is not bit accurate".

